Usage: gprbuild [-P<proj>] [<proj>.gpr] [opts] [name]
    {[-cargs opts] [-cargs:lang opts] [-largs opts] [-kargs opts] [-gargs opts]}

  name is zero or more file names

gprbuild switches:
  --version   Display version and exit
  --help      Display usage and exit

  --no-project
           Do not use project file
  --distributed=slave1[,slave2]
           Activate the remote/distributed compilations
  --hash=string
           Set an hash string to identified environment
  --slave-env[=name]
           Use a specific slave's environment

  --complete-output
           Display all previous errors and warnings
  --no-complete-output, -n
           Do not store compilation outputs in files

  --config=file.cgpr
           Specify the main config project file name
  --autoconf=file.cgpr
           Specify/create the main config project file name
  --target=targetname
           Specify a target for cross platforms
  --db dir Parse dir as an additional knowledge base
  --db-    Do not load the standard knowledge base
  --implicit-with=filename
           Add the given projects as a dependency on all loaded projects
  --relocate-build-tree[=dir]
           Root obj/lib/exec dirs are current-directory or dir
  --root-dir=dir
           Root directory of obj/lib/exec to relocate
  --src-subdirs=dir
           Prepend <obj>/dir to the list of source dirs for each project
  --subdirs=dir
           Use dir as suffix to obj/lib/exec directories
  --getrusage=file
           Print getrusage call results into file
  --single-compile-per-obj-dir
           No simultaneous compilations for the same obj dir
  --build-script=script_file
           Create build script script_file
  --no-indirect-imports
           Sources can import only from directly imported projects
  --indirect-imports
           Sources can import from directly and indirectly imported projects
  --RTS=<runtime>
           Use runtime <runtime> for language Ada
  --RTS:<lang>=<runtime>
           Use runtime <runtime> for language <lang>
  --unchecked-shared-lib-imports
           Shared lib projects may import any project
  --no-object-check
           Do not check object files
  --no-sal-binding
           Reuse binder files when linking SALs
  --restricted-to-languages=<list of languages>
           Restrict the languages of the sources

  --create-map-file
           Create map file mainprog.map
  --create-map-file=mapfile
           Create map file mapfile
  --source-info=<filename>
           Specify/create the project sources cache file
  --keep-temp-files
           Do not delete temporary files

  --autodetect-jobserver
           Autodetect GNU make jobserver and attempt to share job slots

  -aP dir  Add directory dir to project search path
  -b       Bind only
  -c       Compile only
  -d       Display compilation progress
  -eInn    Index of main unit in multi-unit source file
  -eL      Follow symbolic links when processing project files
  -eS      (no action, for compatibility with gnatmake only)
  -f       Force recompilations
  -F       Full project path name in brief error messages
  -j<num>    Use <num> processes to compile, bind, and link
  -jc<num>    Use <num> processes to compile
  -jb<num>    Use <num> processes to bind
  -jl<num>    Use <num> processes to link
  -k       Keep going after compilation errors
  -l       Link only
  -m       Minimum Ada recompilation
  -m2      Checksum based Ada recompilation
  -o name  Choose an alternate executable name
  -p       Create missing obj, lib and exec dirs
  -P proj  Use Project File proj
  -q       Be quiet/terse
  -r       Recursive (default except when using -c)
  -R       Do not use run path option
  -s       Recompile if compiler switches have changed
  -u       Unique compilation, only compile the given files
  -U       Unique compilation for all sources of all projects
  -v       Verbose output
  -vl      Verbose output (low verbosity)
  -vm      Verbose output (medium verbosity)
  -vh      Verbose output (high verbosity)
  -vPx     Specify verbosity when parsing Project Files (x = 0/1/2)
  -we      Treat all warnings as errors
  -wn      Treat warnings as warnings
  -ws      Suppress all gprbuild-specific warnings
  -x       Always create include path file
  -Xnm=val Specify an external reference for Project Files

  -z       No main subprogram (zero main)
  --compiler-subst=lang,tool    Specify alternate compiler
  --compiler-pkg-subst=pkg    Specify alternate package


  -cargs opts    opts are passed to all compilers
  -cargs:<lang> opts
                 opts are passed to the compiler for language <lang> 
  -bargs opts    opts are passed to all binders
  -bargs:<lang> opts
                 opts are passed to the binder for language <lang> 
  -largs opts    opts are passed to the linker
  -kargs opts    opts are passed to gprconfig
  -gargs opts    opts directly interpreted by gprbuild
  -margs opts    equivalent to -gargs opts

For compatibility with gnatmake, these switches are passed to the Ada compiler:
  -nostdlib
  -nostdinc
  -fstack-check
  -fno-inline
  -gxxx
  -Oxx


Report bugs to support@adacore.com
